WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.120
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:05.040
<i>Now, we shall return anew
to the topic of Ougi Oshino.</i>

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.210
<i>That said, she is who she is after all.</i>

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.130
<i>She's nothing more than herself,</i>

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:13.510
<i>so even if I start, even if I start anew,
even if I go back...</i>

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.350
<i>The fundamental topic ends just like that.</i>

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.220
OUGI OSHINO

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:21.020
<i>If I were to write out an existence
such as Ougi Oshino in a novel,</i>

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:24.150
<i>it would come to an end
with just one line.</i>

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.070
<i>"Ougi Oshino was Ougi Oshino...</i>

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.440
<i>...and everyone lived
happily ever after." One line!</i>

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:36.870
<i>And so, we've had a few math classes in a row,
but at the end, let's have a Japanese class.</i>

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.040
<i>Here's a Japanese problem.</i>

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.080
<i>Write about such-and-such.
You must answer within so many words.</i>

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.500
<i>If it's about Ougi Oshino,
just like what I mentioned before.</i>

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:49.670
<i>If you were to put her as the main subject
of the problem, it would read:</i>

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.380
<i>"Describe Ougi Oshino in four words or less."</i>

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.760
<i>and the answer would be "Ougi Oshino."</i>

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.510
<i>So, the final problem I submit to you is this:</i>

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.810
<i>"Just how foolish is Koyomi Araragi?
Answer within twenty words.</i>

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.820
<i>However, you must use the words 'Ougi Oshino'
at least once in your answer."</i>

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:12.490
OWARIMONOGATARI

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:13.990
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST, PART ONE

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:14.490
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.620
In the end...
Did you figure it out, Araragi?

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:21.490
I mean, the reason why Oikura knew about
the occupation of your parents, Araragi.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.790
Yeah. I figured it out.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.830
I confirmed it with Sengoku too,
so I'm sure of it.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:32.510
No, I don't think that's something
you need to confirm while hanging your head...

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.630
Of course I'd want to hang my head.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:38.680
I couldn't remember,
no matter how hard I tried...

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:42.020
But when I did as you told me to, Hanekawa,
it came to light immediately.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.770
Really, Hanekawa,
you really do know everything.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:49.270
I don't know everything.
I only know what I know.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:55.400
That's why I don't know
exactly what Ougi knows.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:01.240
We're fine, right?
She's not tailing us or anything, right?

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:06.500
Tailing? No,
she's not an assassin or anything.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.250
An assassin?

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.250
Isn't tailing someone
a job for a detective, Araragi?

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:21.350
I think in this case,
I would've preferred if she had followed us.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:24.350
If she had tailed us,
I could've thrown her off the track.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:27.100
Maybe you're being
a bit too nervous about all of this?

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:33.110
No, but Araragi, even if she's not tailing us,
she might have anticipated where we're going.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:38.110
Since the destination is very clear,
there's less risk doing that if she's going to investigate...

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:40.910
You can't ever be too nervous about this.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:47.290
If you're not being too nervous about this, Hanekawa,
you're giving Ougi way too much credit.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:52.090
It may be true that she's Oshino's niece,
and seems to be moderately smart for the most part.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:54.210
But she's still like a child, I guess.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:55.840
She's a first-year.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.050
She still has a feeling of cuteness.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:05.850
Us upperclassmen have the duty
of guiding people like her to not end up like Oshino.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:08.730
And that should be
how we repay Oshino as well.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:11.310
How we repay Oshino, huh...

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.020
Yeah, that's a great thing to keep in mind.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.070
Admirable. So admirable.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:21.780
I totally thought you were head-over-heels again
for yet another new cute underclassman.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.410
"Again"?

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:27.540
Back during the case with Kanbaru,
didn't you end up in a similar situation, Araragi?

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.580
If what you have in mind is how you really feel,
I'd like you to stop.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:34.040
Don't act in ways that are misunderstood
as fawning over underclassmen

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.170
when your own class
is having such a rough time.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:39.050
I'll engrave that onto my heart.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:40.760
Good.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:46.640
To confirm, until you tagged along
on Ougi's fieldwork,

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:50.390
you had forgotten all about your memories
of middle school days with Oikura, right?

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.600
Not at all. It's the reverse.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.110
Ougi accompanied me
when I was doing my fieldwork.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:04:00.610
Ougi basically tagged along
with what I was doing.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:03.740
She merely assisted
in my remembering Oikura.

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:11.000
I guess the idea isn't getting across very well...
Am I not expressing myself properly?

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.920
In my eyes, there's nothing more dangerous
than people like that girl.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.670
Dangerous? Are you talking about Oikura?

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:21.420
See, we're not on the same page.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:25.430
It's as if you're diverting the point
of this conversation on purpose.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:34.850
Well, all right. I'm sure it just means
we can't talk about stuff like this today.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:43.150
Hanekawa, if you mean to say you think
Ougi might feel ill will towards Oikura, that's not it.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:46.120
In the first place,
Ougi has never even met Oikura.

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:49.700
I'm not worried about
anything like that, Araragi.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:55.330
Ougi setting her sights on Oikura?
I'm not worried about something like that one bit.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.500
What I am worried about is...

00:04:57.670 --> 00:04:58.750
...is?

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.920
I mean, it's you, Araragi.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:04.880
Something that you don't understand very well
may have set their sights on you.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.430
Something I don't understand very well?

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:10.720
It may be something... that isn't too good.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:14.270
To be honest, I'm not sure
I can protect you through it all.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:15.400
Protect?

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:19.270
Araragi, you called what happened
during spring break "hell."

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:23.400
But Araragi, your true suffering
may be what's to come.

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:31.410
<i>We, Class President Tsubasa Hanekawa,
and Class Vice-President Koyomi Araragi, arrived...</i>

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:38.290
<i>...at our destination,
the current address for Sodachi Oikura.</i>

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:39.880
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.550
<i>Sodachi Oikura,
former class president,</i>

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:46.340
<i>hasn't shown up to school
on the day after that ordeal.</i>

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:52.350
<i>And, apparently sensing the threatening
atmosphere that was lingering,</i>

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.640
<i>Senjyogahara hasn't come to school
since that day either.</i>

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:01.360
And so, Araragi, I'm thinking of going to visit her
after school today...

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:04.490
I mean, visit Senjyogahara and Oikura.

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:09.120
In any case, we don't have enough time,
so I think we should split up and get to it.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:11.790
Senjyogahara or Oikura...

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.540
Araragi, which person do you want to visit?

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:18.120
You can go ahead and choose, Araragi.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:19.000
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:23.170
<i>Visit one's lover...</i>

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:24.960
<i>...or visit one's mortal enemy.</i>

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:30.930
<i>It was quite the ultimate decision,
but I decided on choosing the latter.</i>

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:34.890
<i>The reason why we decided
on splitting up and acting separately,</i>

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:37.270
<i>yet I met up with Hanekawa again later?</i>

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:37.890
HER PASSION

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:39.770
<i>The reasoning is due to
these circumstances.</i>

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.860
Huh? If it isn't Araragi-senpai!

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:46.740
Oh... Ougi.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.910
Ougi, are you going home now?

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:53.330
Going home? Well... No.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.290
What are you talking about, Araragi-senpai?

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:59.420
We had promised to meet here.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:05.090
We made a promise to meet
at 3:42 at the school gates.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.420
Nothing less from you, Araragi-senpai.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:12.470
You're right on time. You're so precise.
You're really faithful in that way....

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:14.220
...you fool.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.560
Hurray, I'm so happy.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:23.610
Araragi-senpai is going to take me now
to eat non-revolving sushi.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:25.900
Did I make such a promise?!

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:29.150
You did indeed. You said it was
to celebrate my transferring to this school.

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:32.410
Non-revolving sushi
to celebrate a school transfer...

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.490
What in the world
just transferred into my school?

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:45.210
I'm sorry, Ougi. Unfortunately,
I don't think I can keep my promise with you.

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:48.420
My, what is that
handsome-sounding line for?

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:51.130
Saying such a handsome-sounding line
while breaking a promise

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:53.090
must mean that you don't have
any money on you.

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:57.470
I have to take a bit of time now
to head to Oikura's house, Ougi.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:01.100
Oh? So you're going to go
to that ruined house again?

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:04.110
No, not the ruined house,
but her current address...

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:04.860
NO.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.320
I'VE BECOME WAY TOO TALKATIVE
IN FRONT OF OUGI

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:17.700
What are you doing?

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:20.580
Well, I tried opening the zipper
that was on your mouth.

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:24.130
Though, it was more like Velcro
than a zipper...

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:27.800
Do tell me a bit more about this, please.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.130
What happened?

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:35.800
You're working on winning Oikura-senpai over
at amazing speed. Such rapid progress.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:39.890
Report on just how things developed
and in what manner, fool.

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:43.140
No, it's not like winning her over
or anything like that.

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:47.320
It's not like I'm going to visit in order to see her,
but it's more like barging in on my part.

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:50.570
She didn't come to school again yesterday.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:53.150
And even the day before that,
it was basically the same as being absent...

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:54.450
I WAS FORCED TO EXPLAIN.

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:56.570
And that's how it is.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.410
So that's how it is?

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:01.660
I didn't hear much
about the details yet,

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:05.380
but she seems to be
living apart from her parents now.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:07.380
Apart from her parents?

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:11.920
I see, then she was taken
into protective custody by a relative?

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:14.180
No, apparently she lives on her own.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.300
I see... That's also interesting.

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:21.560
So just like you said, Ougi,

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:25.270
something along the lines of
her parents divorcing happened five years ago.

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:27.560
I guess you could say
her family was shattered.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:29.940
And she returned here two years ago.

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:33.820
I see... The sleuthing I did
without much thought at all was correct.

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:38.910
However, Araragi-senpai...
Foolish Araragi-senpai...

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:41.830
In other words, Araragi-senpai,
you're about to go visit a girl

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:45.210
who is in reality
living all by herself.

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:48.960
That's not good.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:50.960
It's not good?

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:53.210
It's not good, not good at all.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.800
That's an act unbefitting a gentleman.

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:59.510
For a boy to make a solitary visit
to a girl living alone?

00:09:59.510 --> 00:10:02.720
It wouldn't be surprising if someone suspects
there's some relationship there.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:05.940
That isn't an act someone with a partner
should be doing.

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:12.320
Though your resolve seems to be strong.

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:16.280
And I was looking forward
to non-revolving sushi...

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:18.320
See you, Ougi.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.320
Oh, I know!

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:22.580
I just thought of something brilliant,
Araragi-senpai.

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:27.330
Yours truly, though unworthy,
shall accompany you on this house call.

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.590
You, Ougi? That is a welcome offer...

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:33.340
HMM? IS IT WELCOME?

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:36.630
In other words,
it just has to be more than one person.

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:39.510
Especially because, you know, I'm a girl.

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:43.390
My being there with you should
calm down Oikura-senpai's heart somewhat.

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:47.270
She's not one to calm down
just because she's dealing with girls...

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:51.310
WOULD SHE CALM DOWN EVEN A LITTLE BIT
IF IT WAS AN UNDERCLASSMAN?

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:55.740
And as you're fully aware,
I'm very adept at listening to others.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:11:00.200
Perhaps I may be able to draw out
all sorts of things from Oikura-senpai.

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:01.570
Draw out...

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:06.500
Araragi-senpai, until now,
your recollection of that class assembly

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:09.540
or the summer break
of your 7th grade year,

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:12.210
allowed you to remember
how she was in the past.

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:16.210
However, you haven't been able
to properly speak to her current self at all.

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:20.470
I can offer myself as the middleman
so there won't be any arguments.

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:26.640
I mean, I've already come this far, right?

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:28.980
Please let me do this service.

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:38.860
Then, Ougi, I request that you do.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.110
Yes, it's been requested of me.

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:43.490
You shouldn't make that request!

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:52.460
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:55.960
You shouldn't make that request, Araragi.

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:57.710
Hanekawa...

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:00.720
You shouldn't.

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:04.600
See, you shouldn't rope in an underclassman
to an internal dispute of our class.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:06.640
OH. SO THAT'S WHAT YOU MEAN?
THAT'S WHAT THIS IS?

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:07.350
INDEED, IT'S NOT A GOOD THING
TO ROPE OUTSIDERS INTO A PRIVATE AFFAIR.

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:08.520
Ougi—

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.190
No, no.

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:13.810
Don't be modest with me
in a strange manner, Araragi-senpai.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:15.980
I would be hurt more by that.

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:20.950
Please don't worry about me at all.
I don't mind at all.

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:22.740
So please don't mind me.

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:27.080
It's more like being told something so distant
at this point in time is what's shocking.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:28.910
It's like, disappointing.

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:35.790
We have that kind of relationship
between us, Araragi-senpai.

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:40.420
What kind of a relationship
do you and Araragi have, huh?

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:47.350
You met Araragi for the very first time
a mere three days ago, correct?

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:50.600
Yes, correct.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:55.060
But, well, relationships between people
aren't necessarily measured by time.

00:12:55.900 --> 00:13:01.530
I thought that I had really hit it off well
with Araragi-senpai in such a short amount of time.

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:03.860
We were locked inside
a mysterious classroom together.

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.070
We went on an adventure
in a ruined house together.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:10.330
We shared experiences that were
impossible in normal life together, so...

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:13.040
Right, Araragi-senpai?

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:15.210
Yeah, that's right.

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:17.460
Oh, yes.

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:19.710
I've heard about those ordeals.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:24.880
It seems my dear friend Araragi has received
a great deal of assistance in that regard.

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:32.680
I had thought that I needed
to give my thanks for that.

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:34.810
But well....

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:37.110
If it were me instead of you,
I would've done it a lot better.

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:42.110
I see.

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:44.110
I see, indeed.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:47.870
Right. Yes, indeed, there's no doubt
you would've done things much better than I did.

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:50.620
As everyone knows, you're a genius.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:54.580
Yes, of course, I've heard all about it
from my uncle as well.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:58.130
By "uncle," are you
perhaps referring to Oshino?

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:01.130
Yes, as I'm his niece.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:07.140
But, well... Even that ingenious nature
is meaningless if it cannot be exhibited.

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:11.640
In reality, I was the one that was
next to Araragi-senpai when everything happened.

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:16.020
Your ingenious nature
that even my uncle was afraid of...

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:21.520
Yes, but still, if I look at you from that perspective,
you really aren't as good as I've heard you are.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:25.150
If you are the Tsubasa Hanekawa
that I had heard so much of...

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:29.820
You never would've been absent for the perils
that Araragi-senpai faced.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:35.330
By saying "I would've done it a lot better,"
don't you actually mean, "If I was in my prime"?

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:37.120
Come on, Ougi.

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:39.790
That's not a nice way of saying things.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:42.420
There are things that you can say,
and things you shouldn't.

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:44.800
What about Hanekawa
are you saying you know?

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:47.630
I don't know anything.

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:51.600
It's what you know, Araragi-senpai.

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:55.430
About Hanekawa-senpai's past and present...

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:58.190
...and about her future.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:06.030
Right. On that point, this is essentially
something I shouldn't interfere with.

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:11.410
Well, Hanekawa-senpai,
I'm not stupid enough to go against you directly.

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:17.040
I wouldn't want to be rude to you
and be hated by my beloved Araragi-senpai, either.

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:20.920
So please, let's proceed from here
by utilizing compartmentalization.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:24.090
Now, excuse me.
Please, go on ahead.

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:27.380
You're going to head to Senjyogahara-senpai's house
to visit her right now, right?

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:31.680
That house seems to be further away,
so shouldn't you hurry over there?

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:33.180
"Further away"?

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:36.310
Please rest assured.

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:39.350
If it's the case that you don't want
to see your valued friend Araragi-senpai

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:43.060
ask a favor from an underclassman,

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:45.110
I'll make sure it's not like that.

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:48.610
I mean, this is something
that I suggested in the first place.

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:53.280
I can make it so that I'm following
Araragi-senpai's exact footsteps of my own accord.

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:55.540
Much like some spirit possessing him.

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:58.000
That way, it won't bother you, right?

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:00.710
See, you know, it can be like
what you often read in mystery novels -

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.540
the assistant who forces himself
into that role.

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:04.380
An assistant forcing himself
into that role...

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:07.090
If Araragi-senpai is troubled
for one reason or another,

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:09.220
I can't just leave him alone like that.

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:13.260
I want to be one that saves Araragi-senpai.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:18.180
Wasn't it the case that "all people can do
is save themselves on their own"?

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:20.850
That's my uncle's stance.

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:23.940
My stance is more along the lines
of the old "Grateful Crane" story.

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:25.690
The Grateful Crane?

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:29.780
Well, I wouldn't mind if it was
the "Straw Hats on the Jizo Statues" story either.

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:32.780
Simply put, my policy is
overdoing a show of gratitude.

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:36.080
Like one where I'm told,
"You're showing too much gratitude!"

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:41.460
Araragi-senpai has been exceptionally kind to me
as I transferred to this school,

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:45.290
and I feel I should show my gratitude in return,
even if it means putting my life on the line.

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:51.760
Araragi, I'm changing plans.

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:54.680
I'll go to Oikura's place as well.

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:56.550
I'll go with you, Araragi.

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:02.230
That way, you don't have
anything to complain about, right?

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:09.820
Ougi, you were saying that Araragi, a boy,
going alone to Oikura's place would be a problem.

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:13.660
If I went together with him,
that leaves no issues in that regard.

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:15.030
And you have no excuse.

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:17.780
Correct?

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:20.910
Aside from whether or not
there's a problem...

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:26.920
Weren't you supposed to visit Senjyogahara-senpai's
place as well, Hanekawa-senpai?

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:31.880
That's far from laudable behavior,
to leave your close friend for later.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:36.550
I figured my chat with Senjyogahara
would be a long one to begin with.

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:38.760
I'll just stay over at her place tonight.

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:43.230
I think we'll have the first pajama party
in a while at Senjyogahara's place.

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:43.980
PAJAMA PARTY?

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:45.850
That settles that, right?

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:49.940
Because.... I can do things
better than you can.

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:53.700
In this world, it's not about whether or not
things can be done well, either.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:57.740
Doing things too well
can lack balance in its own way.

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:00.870
Because it won't end up
as a happy medium like that.

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:04.330
I figure you're fully aware of that.

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:07.580
Well, good or bad aside,

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:11.130
it's not me that decides this.
It's Araragi-senpai.

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:17.300
Whether you go with me,
or go with Hanekawa-senpai.

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:20.470
Araragi-senpai,
you should be the one to decide.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:22.520
The power to decide is in your hands.

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:27.310
Both myself and Hanekawa-senpai
will abide by your decision.

00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:28.400
Right?

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:31.150
You're right. Araragi, you decide for us.

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:33.650
Because this isn't something
I can force upon you.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:39.950
You know, Araragi-senpai.

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:44.290
It's such a bad thing to make Hanekawa-senpai,
a valued person you're indebted to,

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:47.500
trouble someone else
for a personal reason.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:51.750
If she's saying this is private,
then Hanekawa-senpai is also out of the loop.

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:57.260
Araragi-senpai, you'd never wish for something
that would trouble Hanekawa-senpai, right?

00:18:57.930 --> 00:18:58.930
HMM, THAT IS, INDEED, QUITE CORRECT.

00:18:58.930 --> 00:18:59.840
THIS GIRL REALLY SAYS THINGS
THAT ARE CORRECT.

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:04.470
I promise you, Araragi-senpai.
If you let me come with you,

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:09.480
no matter what kind of mystery there is,
I'll show you an answer to it yet again.

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:10.480
WELL, IF YOU'RE GOING TO GO THAT FAR
WITH YOUR STATEMENTS...

00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:15.610
I promise you, Araragi.

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:18.360
If you decide you want to come with me...

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:23.160
...I'll let you touch my breasts.

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:25.250
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:31.580
So room 444 in this place, huh...

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:35.880
It looks like the management company
isn't all too attentive.

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:38.680
This looks more like
a housing complex than condos.

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:42.760
Oikura is probably
receiving some sort of aid.

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:43.390
Aid?

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:48.230
From officials. And that's how
they introduced her to this property, I think.

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:53.190
<i>What I further found out was how Oikura and I
first met back when we were in grade school...</i>

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:58.950
<i>But how did I forget such a thing,
when even Sengoku remembered it?</i>

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:02.200
<i>No, it's not like I ever forgot it...</i>

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:07.250
When I think about it,
I may be cold-hearted.

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:10.670
I mean, I had forgotten
about Sengoku as well,

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:12.830
and I didn't realize who she was
when we first met.

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:18.300
But I think that's something
that can't be helped.

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:27.390
You didn't have an impressionable relationship
with either Sengoku or Oikura, right?

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:31.270
Then, Araragi,
can you wait here for a minute?

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:33.610
Here at the staircase? Why?

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:36.860
I mean, Oikura lives by herself.

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:40.530
So if we were to ring the doorbell
and she comes out in pajamas or loungewear...

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:44.780
She might be embarrassed
if you saw her like that, Araragi.

00:20:50.460 --> 00:20:51.370
Who is it?

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:58.380
<i>So let me ponder again on how
that bloodcurdling confrontation was structured...</i>

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:02.930
<i>Many people may perhaps
be misunderstanding me,</i>

00:21:02.930 --> 00:21:09.020
<i>but it's not that I chose Hanekawa as my partner
over Ougi because I was drawn to her breasts.</i>

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:12.440
<i>I felt something something was highly unusual
with the current situation</i>

00:21:12.440 --> 00:21:14.520
<i>if it made Hanekawa go so far
as to say that.</i>

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:18.150
<i>That's why, with the choice between the two,
I chose her as my partner.</i>

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:21.440
<i>I did feel bad for Ougi, though.</i>

00:21:21.820 --> 00:21:23.660
<i>I should properly follow through with her.</i>

00:21:23.660 --> 00:21:26.370
<i>I need to be someone that can
do things like that as well from now on.</i>

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:32.830
<i>That's right. Putting non-revolving sushi aside,
I can take her to a place with revolving sushi...</i>

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:36.920
Araragi, it's fine for you to come up now.

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:38.960
Come up? But...

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:41.420
She said it's okay for us to go in.

00:21:41.590 --> 00:21:47.050
However, to give you spoilers in advance,
she's still in her pajamas.

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:52.100
Wait, weren't you trying
to avoid such a situation?

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:56.810
She said, "I don't want to make such an effort
as to change into clothes just because Araragi is here."

00:21:57.310 --> 00:22:01.570
I tried my best to convince her otherwise,
but the more I talked, the more stubborn she became.

00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:03.900
In the end, she said
she will absolutely not change clothes,

00:22:03.900 --> 00:22:06.410
and that if I said anything more,
she'd greet us naked.

00:22:06.410 --> 00:22:07.660
So I decided to back down.

00:22:08.070 --> 00:22:14.580
Rest assured, even I wouldn't be so frivolous
as to be elated over a girl in pajamas in this situation.

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:15.670
I don't know about that.

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:18.920
After all, this is coming from the person
who's after me for my breasts.

00:22:20.170 --> 00:22:21.380
THE ACTUAL PERSON INVOLVED
REALIZES HOW I FELT THE LEAST.

00:22:21.800 --> 00:22:25.760
<i>Now that the gate has been opened,
we have no choice but to step inside.</i>

00:22:26.050 --> 00:22:29.220
<i>Even if it's like the castle gates opening
as a declaration of war,</i>

00:22:29.220 --> 00:22:31.510
<i>I must accept it for what it is.</i>

00:22:31.890 --> 00:22:33.350
<i>Because that is my...</i>

00:22:33.350 --> 00:24:20.141
<i>...my duty as a childhood friend
of Sodachi Oikura.</i>
